// The positive half of KR-69. `@compileFor(ARCH_RISCV64)` is an ERROR with no riscv target in sight
// (tests/xfail/compilefor_unknown_platform.kama) — and the manifest beside this file declares one, so
// the same gate is legal here. That is the whole of what a user does to lift the error, and it is the
// gesture BUILDING for riscv needs anyway.
//
// It buys more than silence: declaring the target brings the gated code into `kama check`'s cover, so
// a type error behind this gate is now FOUND, tagged `[--target RISCV]`. tools/check-compilefor-cover.sh
// asserts that half; this file asserts the build half — the host build keeps the complementary
// declaration and returns 41.
@compileFor(ARCH_RISCV64)
fn int32 platformValue() { return 3; }

@compileFor(!ARCH_RISCV64)
fn int32 platformValue() { return 41; }

fn int32 main() { return platformValue(); }
